      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "For maximizing saturation, the single mega-bolus before sleep is far more aggressive and generally less efficient than controlled splitting. While some claim sleep aids assimilation, the body's absorption mechanisms are best supported by consistent, smaller inputs over time. Split-dosing maintains stable plasma levels, which is superior for sustained adaptation, whereas a single massive dose risks overwhelming the system and leading to rapid clearance. Stick to the calculated split dosing for a truly optimized, high-performance protocol.",
      "source": "target",
