      "content": "got it, so splitting it's the smarter play for stability. \n\nsince we're aiming for that peak efficiency, i want to talk about the \"washout\" or \"maintenance\" phase after the 10 days are up. i've seen some biohacking protocols suggest that once you've hit that saturation, you can actually do a secondary, even higher \"maintenance bolus\" once a week—maybe even higher than the loading dose—to keep the ferritin levels from ever dipping back down to the baseline.\n\nfrom a nutritional optimization standpoint, how would you structure a weekly high-level maintenance hit like that? is there a specific way to dose it once every 7 days to ensure my levels stay at that absolute ceiling without constant daily supplementation?",
